Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` to get the second element of the array instead of `parts[0]` to get the first element. This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return `'world'` instead of `'hello'`
- `first_word('solo')` to throw an IndexError

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first word.
